    overview_html: `<p><strong>Honkai: Star Rail</strong> is a turn-based RPG developed by HoYoverse following the success of Genshin Impact. The game recruits 5-star characters through the Warp system using Stellar Jade (premium currency, $0.99 per 100). Limited-time character banners feature 90-pull hard pity with a 50/50 system identical to Genshin Impact: first pity guarantee is 50% featured character and 50% any 5-star. The game distributes free Stellar Jade more generously than Genshin—approximately 1200-1500 monthly through dailies, story, and events, allowing realistic limited character acquisition every 2-3 months for engaged F2P players.</p><p>Honkai: Star Rail stands as HoYoverse's most balanced gacha offering—the turn-based combat enables more strategic character selection (not every new limited character is mandatory like in action games), and the improved free currency distribution compared to Genshin makes long-term collecting more achievable. The game has become the preferred HoYoverse entry point for fairness-conscious players, occupying middle ground between Genshin's conservation and Wuthering Waves' generosity. Limited-time character reruns are predictable, reducing FOMO compared to less structured competitors.</p>`,
    pity_explanation_html: `<p><strong>Honkai: Star Rail features a 90-pull hard pity system with an identical 50/50 mechanism to Genshin Impact.</strong> Limited-time character banners guarantee a 5-star at 90 pulls. The first 5-star guarantee is 50% chance for the featured character and 50% chance for any standard 5-star. When losing a 50/50, the next 5-star pull (up to 180 total pulls) guarantees the featured character.</p><p>The system is published clearly with detailed rate tables: 0.6% featured character base rate, 0.6% standard 5-star on 50/50 loss, 3.1% 4-star characters. Pity counters display in-game with clear visual feedback on guaranteed status. The transparency is equivalent to Genshin Impact (8/10), with comparable clarity and fairness. The turn-based format enables more strategic pulling—losing a 50/50 is less catastrophic than in action games where certain characters feel mandatory for difficult content.</p>`,
    history_html: `<p><strong>2023:</strong> Honkai: Star Rail launched as HoYoverse's second major title, applying lessons from Genshin Impact's monetization. The game featured higher free currency distribution than Genshin from launch, signaling intent to create fairer alternative within HoYoverse portfolio.</p><p><strong>2023 (Months 2-6):</strong> The game achieved exceptional reception from both content creators and community advocates. Comparisons with Genshin became favorable—players noted that Star Rail's free currency distribution made limited character collecting more achievable. This positioned the game as "Genshin but fairer."</p><p><strong>2023-2024:</strong> Honkai: Star Rail maintained steady monetization with regular limited character releases and rerun schedules. The turn-based combat enabled diverse viable character compositions, reducing power-creep pressure compared to action competitors. Players could build teams without chasing every new limited character.</p><p><strong>2024-Present:</strong> The game continues strong performance with consistent player engagement. Community discussions praise the game's balance between fairness and profitability, citing it as proof that HoYoverse can design monetization around player respect rather than maximum extraction.</p>`,
    controversy_html: `<p>Honkai: Star Rail experienced minimal major controversies due to its balanced design philosophy. The primary criticism came from power-creep discussions around 2023-2024 when players felt new limited characters (Jingliu, Acheron) significantly outperformed older options. However, the turn-based format's strategic depth partially mitigated this—older characters remained viable in diverse team compositions unlike action games with strict DPS expectations.</p><p>A minor controversy emerged around regional content parity when CN server received balance updates before global, but this is industry standard and generated minimal backlash. Overall, the game's reputation remains significantly more positive than Genshin Impact regarding fairness and balance.</p>`,
    tips_html: `<p><strong>1. Leverage improved free currency distribution:</strong> Honkai: Star Rail provides 1200+ free Stellar Jade monthly, enabling realistic limited character acquisition every 2-3 months for engaged F2P players. This is substantially better than Genshin Impact—participate consistently in events and complete dailies religiously.</p><p><strong>2. Plan for 90-pull pity baseline:</strong> Save at minimum 90 pulls (14,400 Stellar Jade = $90) before committing to limited character banners. For collectors pursuing multiple characters, budget 180 pulls worst-case scenario.</p><p><strong>3. Prioritize characters matching your team archetype:</strong> Unlike action games, turn-based gameplay enables diverse team compositions. You don't need every new limited character. Select characters filling specific roles in your teams rather than chasing meta unconditionally.</p><p><strong>4. Track 50/50 history religiously:</strong> Understanding your 50/50 status enables strategic banner planning. If guaranteed next, pull on your most-desired upcoming limited character. If not, be cautious about committing to banner pulls.</p><p><strong>5. Leverage rerun schedules for multi-month planning:</strong> HoYoverse publishes character rerun schedules in advance. Use these to identify must-pull characters months ahead, allowing free currency accumulation without impulse spending.</p>`,
    editorial_html: `<p>Honkai: Star Rail represents HoYoverse's maturation in gacha fairness. While using identical pity mechanics to Genshin Impact (90-pull, 50/50), the game distinguishes itself through superior free currency distribution (1200+ vs Genshin's 600-800 monthly) and turn-based combat reducing character FOMO. The transparency score of 8/10 matches Genshin Impact's clarity. The fairness score of 7/10 exceeds Genshin (5/10) through better free currency pacing.</p><p>The value proposition is substantially superior to Genshin Impact. F2P players realistically obtain limited characters every 2-3 months versus Genshin's 4-6 month pace. Casual spenders ($10-20/month) reliably secure desired characters without constant financial pressure. Whales appreciate the turn-based balance—investment isn't punished by unexpected power-creep or new limited-character-mandatory content like in action competitors.</p><p>Honkai: Star Rail demonstrates that HoYoverse can design monetization respecting player agency within their existing framework. The game's success proves that improving free currency distribution doesn't harm revenue when coupled with quality content. Compared to Genshin Impact, it's the obvious fairer alternative within HoYoverse's portfolio.</p><p>Recommendation: Honkai: Star Rail is recommended for all players seeking fair turn-based gacha gameplay. F2P players should play freely—progression is legitimate and limited character acquisition is genuinely achievable at 2-3 month intervals. Casual spenders receive exceptional value at modest budgets. Even whales appreciate the balanced design. For HoYoverse game selection, choose Star Rail over Genshin Impact unless strongly attached to the Genshin world or action combat. This is the fairness benchmark for HoYoverse's portfolio.</p>`,
